From ad0eac34170097417010250619079829a489734c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ESP32-S31 Linux <s31-linux@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hci: trust the selected integrated Classic profile

The S31 controller-only firmware reports the No BR/EDR feature bit even when
its dual-mode Classic controller is built and enabled.  Bluedroid selects its
host behavior from the integrated build configuration; do the same for this
dedicated BTstack Classic appliance so the normal GAP scan tasks are issued.

This policy does not rewrite controller feature events or special-case any HCI
command response.
---
 src/hci.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hci.c b/src/hci.c
index 594b51568..961873c4a 100644
--- a/src/hci.c
+++ b/src/hci.c
@@ -1538 +1538,5 @@ bool hci_classic_supported(void){
-    return (hci_stack->local_supported_features[4] & (1 << 5)) == 0;
+#ifdef S31_BTSTACK_FORCE_CLASSIC
+    return true;
+#else
+    return (hci_stack->local_supported_features[4] & (1 << 5)) == 0;
+#endif
